{"name":"Holly Glen","hex":"#a2b7b5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"holly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various shrubs or (mostly) small trees, of the genus Ilex, either evergreen or deciduous, used as decoration especially at Christmas.","The wood from this tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holly"},{"term":"glen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A secluded and narrow valley, especially one with a river running through it; a depression between hills; a dale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Holly","blocks":[{"text":"Ilex or holly is a genus of over 570 species of flowering plants in the family Aquifoliaceae, and the only living genus in that family. Ilex has the most species of any woody dioecious angiosperm genus. The species are evergreen or deciduous trees, shrubs, and climbers from tropics to temperate zones worldwide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Ilex-aquifolium_%28Europaeische_Stechpalme-1%29.jpg/330px-Ilex-aquifolium_%28Europaeische_Stechpalme-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holly","wikidata":"Q117085"},{"title":"Glen","blocks":[{"text":"A glen is a valley, typically one that is long and bounded by gently sloped concave sides, unlike a ravine, which is deep and bounded by steep slopes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Glendun_-_geograph.org.uk_-_465779.jpg/330px-Glendun_-_geograph.org.uk_-_465779.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glen","wikidata":"Q1976531"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Ilex_paraguariensis_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-074.jpg/330px-Ilex_paraguariensis_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-074.jpg?utm_source=en.wik